1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:03,315
Hi again. In previous courses,

2
00:00:03,315 --> 00:00:05,280
we've discussed the
importance of breaking

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:07,230
your project down into milestones

4
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:08,940
and tasks and assigning

5
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:11,610
those tasks to different
members of your team.

6
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:15,090
We've also discussed setting
a schedule and budget.

7
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:18,180
But once the project
execution phase gets going,

8
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:21,210
how do you actually know that
the work is getting done?

9
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:24,380
Well, you can do this in a
few ways, but primarily,

10
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:25,670
you can keep tabs on

11
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:28,415
project progress by
tracking and measurement.

12
00:00:28,415 --> 00:00:31,600
This is actually a big part
of project management.

13
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,160
Tracking, by definition,
is a method of

14
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,910
following the progress of
a project's activities.

15
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:38,480
Measuring project performance

16
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,820
regularly to identify deviations

17
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:42,620
from the project plan can help

18
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:44,935
ensure that the project
stays on track.

19
00:00:44,935 --> 00:00:47,045
A deviation is anything that

20
00:00:47,045 --> 00:00:49,445
alters your original
course of action.

21
00:00:49,445 --> 00:00:51,290
Deviations from the project plan

22
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:53,210
can be positive or negative.

23
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,760
Are you ahead of schedule
because a technical problem

24
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,860
is less complex than you
estimated? Thumbs up.

25
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:01,700
Did a natural disaster shut
down your testing team?

26
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,595
Big thumbs down.

27
00:01:03,595 --> 00:01:06,320
Both of these are
examples of deviations.

28
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,720
They're also examples
of why tracking is

29
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,430
such a crucial part of your role

30
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:12,590
during the project
execution phase.

31
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:14,660
Let's examine some
of the ways that

32
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,615
tracking is beneficial for
your project's success.

33
00:01:17,615 --> 00:01:21,260
To start, tracking makes
key project information

34
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,450
transparent, and transparency is

35
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:25,595
essential for accurate
decision-making.

36
00:01:25,595 --> 00:01:27,860
Even the strongest
project managers make

37
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:31,015
poor decisions when they
lack information or context.

38
00:01:31,015 --> 00:01:33,950
Tracking centralizes
project information so that

39
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:35,780
everyone can
understand the status

40
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,160
of each part of the project,

41
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:40,385
which can then help you identify
gaps in your knowledge.

42
00:01:40,385 --> 00:01:43,490
Also, projects have so
many little details.

43
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:45,515
It's hard to keep
everything straight.

44
00:01:45,515 --> 00:01:47,240
Tracking helps ensure that

45
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,150
you don't risk
forgetting something.

46
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,035
Second, tracking helps keep

47
00:01:51,035 --> 00:01:52,490
all team members and stakeholders

48
00:01:52,490 --> 00:01:54,190
in touch with
deadlines and goals.

49
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:55,850
To ensure that everyone has

50
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:57,964
visibility into project progress,

51
00:01:57,964 --> 00:01:59,810
you should have a
project plan that

52
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:02,680
works both for you and your team.

53
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:05,030
This way you're all
on the same page

54
00:02:05,030 --> 00:02:06,919
about how the project
is progressing.

55
00:02:06,919 --> 00:02:08,780
You will learn about
different ways to

56
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:10,985
track a project later
in this module.

57
00:02:10,985 --> 00:02:13,730
Tracking is also
crucial for recognizing

58
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:16,600
risks and issues that can
derail your progress.

59
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:18,500
With effective tracking, you will

60
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:20,300
be able to identify issues in

61
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,280
a timely fashion and work with

62
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,410
your team to take
corrective action.

63
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:26,180
By providing visibility into

64
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:27,940
the various parts of the project,

65
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:30,005
tracking helps you and your team

66
00:02:30,005 --> 00:02:33,005
identify and focus
on areas at risk.

67
00:02:33,005 --> 00:02:35,750
And finally, tracking helps
build confidence that

68
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:38,300
the project is set to
be delivered on time,

69
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:40,315
in-scope, and within budget.

70
00:02:40,315 --> 00:02:42,140
Having a clear, up-to-date

71
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:44,270
picture of the overall
project status

72
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:45,770
keeps the team motivated and

73
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:47,785
focused on staying the course.

74
00:02:47,785 --> 00:02:50,240
So to recap, tracking
is important for

75
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:52,700
a few key reasons,
like transparency,

76
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:55,925
risk management, and keeping
the project on track.

77
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:57,260
Coming up, we'll take you

78
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,550
through some of the key items to

79
00:02:58,550 --> 00:03:02,580
track during project
execution. Meet you there.
